# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# SDR captures: ELRS Find sweeps save to captures/elrs_find_*/. We SYNC the
# lightweight per-channel METADATA (.meta.txt + manifest/.json) via git so the
# other session sees what a sweep found and with what parameters — but NOT the
# raw IQ. A single .complex8 is ~2 MB and a full 80-channel sweep is ~160 MB; at
# that rate git history bloats fast (it was ~350 MB of mostly noise/dropped
# captures). Raw IQ stays LOCAL by default.
#   When a capture actually has an ELRS hit worth remote deep-analysis, force-add
#   just that channel's file:  git add -f captures/elrs_find_<ts>/ch<N>_*.complex8
# Everything that looks like a stray capture outside captures/ stays ignored too.
*.iq
*.complex8
*.cf32
*.jsonl
!captures/
!captures/**/
!captures/**/*.meta.txt
!captures/**/*.json
!captures/**/manifest.json

# C++ build artifacts (cpp/build.sh produces these)
cpp/elrs_intercept
cpp/tests/test_elrs_decode
cpp/tests/test_lora_demod
cpp/test_elrs_decode
cpp/test_lora_demod
cpp/*.bin
cpp/*.o

# Tarballs / archives — never commit
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Scan output (regenerated)
scan.jsonl
